mpanies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [801, 1596, 1441, 1761], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"a Source: Federal Reserve Board Treasury International Capital Survey. Includes nonmarketable foreign series, Treasury securities, and Treasury deposit funds. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Estimates reflect the 1989 benchmark to 1994, the 1994 benchmark to September 2001, the March 2000 benchmark to September 2002, the June 2002 benchmark to December 2003, the June 2003 benchmark to March 2004, the June 2004 benchmark to March 2005, the June 2005 benchmark to February 2006, and the June 2006 benchmark to February 2007. For additional information see: http://www.treas.gov/tic/ticsec2.shtml.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [803, 1761, 1443, 1798], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"9 Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1331, 2053, 1492, 2077], \"page_id\": 48}], \"content\": \"September 2007\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 97, 178, 125], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"42\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [534, 210, 1096, 250], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 269, 803, 361], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The table in this section presents yields on Treasury marketable securities for maturities ranging from 1 month to 30 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 368, 803, 679], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes, and bonds. These Constant Maturity Treasury rates (CMTs) are interpolated from the Treasury yield curve and published daily at Treasury's Domestic Finance web site, www.ustreas.gov/offices/domestic-finance/debt-management/interest-rate/ yield.shtml. The yield curve is fitted daily using a hermite cubic spline. For inputs, Treasury primarily uses the bid yields of the on-the-run securities (most recently auctioned Treasury securities in all maturity tranches that Treasury currently auctions) as\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 269, 1494, 394], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"quoted in the secondary bond market as of approximately 3:30 p.m. each trading day. CMT yields are based on semiannual interest payments and are read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 403, 1494, 552], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"The quotations used by Treasury to calculate the bid yields and fit the yield curve are obtained by the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System also publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 561, 1494, 686], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"Treasury discontinued the 30-year constant maturity yield during the time period February 18, 2002, through February 8, 2006. Thus, 30-year yields for that time frame are not available.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [319, 771, 1288, 842], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities: Bills, Notes, and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [413, 853, 1191, 884], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"[In percentages. Source: Office of Debt Management, Office of the Under Secretary for Domestic Finance]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 884, 1472, 1787], \"page_id\": 49}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th>1-mo. (1)</th><th>3-mo. (2)</th><th>6-mo. (3)</th><th>1-yr. (4)</th><th>2-yr. (5)</th><th>3-yr. (6)</th><th>5-yr. (7)</th><th>7-yr. (8)</th><th>10-yr. (9)</th><th>20-yr. (10)</th><th>30-yr. (11)</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"12\\\">Monthly average:</td></tr><tr><td>2006 - July</td><td>4.90</td><td>5.08</td><td>5.27</td><td>5.22</td><td>5.12</td><td>5.07</td><td>5.04</td><td>5.05</td><td>5.09</td><td>5.25</td><td>5.13</td></tr><tr><td>Aug</td><td>5.16</td><td>5.09</td><td>5.17</td><td>5.08</td><td>4.90</td><td>4.85</td><td>4.82</td><td>4.83</td><td>4.88</td><td>5.08</td><td>5.00</td></tr><tr><td>Sept</td><td>4.77</td><td>4.93</td><td>5.08</td><td>4.97</td><td>4.77</td><td>4.69</td><td>4.67</td><td>4.68</td><td>4.72</td><td>4.93</td><td>4.85</td></tr><tr><td>Oct</td><td>4.97</td><td>5.05</td><td>5.12</td><td>5.01</td><td>4.80</td><td>4.72</td><td>4.69</td><td>4.69</td><td>4.73</td><td>4.94</td><td>4.85</td></tr><tr><td>Nov</td><td>5.21</td><td>5.07</td><td>5.15</td><td>5.01</td><td>4.74</td><td>4.64</td><td>4.58</td><td>4.58</td><td>4.60</td><td>4.78</td><td>4.69</td></tr><tr><td>Dec</td><td>4.87</td><td>4.97</td><td>5.07</td><td>4.94</td><td>4.67</td><td>4.58</td><td>4.53</td><td>4.54</td><td>4.56</td><td>4.78</td><td>4.68</td></tr><tr><td>2007 - Jan</td><td>4.94</td><td>5.11</td><td>5.15</td><td>5.06</td><td>4.88</td><td>4.79</td><td>4.75</td><td>4.75</td><td>4.76</td><td>4.95</td><td>4.85</td></tr><tr><td>Feb</td><td>5.18</td><td>5.16</td><td>5.16</td><td>5.05</td><td>4.85</td><td>4.75</td><td>4.71</td><td>4.71</td><td>4.72</td><td>4.93</td><td>4.82</td></tr><tr><td>Mar<