6}], \"content\": \"700\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [406, 217, 1224, 248], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Exchange Stabilization Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 269, 794, 474], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"To stabilize the exchange value of the dollar, the Exchange Stabilization Fund (ESF) was established pursuant to chapter 6, section 10 of the Gold Reserve Act of January 30, 1934 (codified at 31 United States Code 5302), which authorized establishment of a Treasury fund to be operated under the exclusive control of the Secretary, with approval of the President.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 490, 792, 578], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Subsequent amendment of the Gold Reserve Act modified the original purpose somewhat to reflect termination of the fixed exchange rate system.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 592, 796, 768], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Resources of the fund include dollar balances, partially invested in U.S. Government securities, special drawing rights (SDRs), and balances of foreign currencies. Principal sources of income (+) or loss (-) for the fund are profits (+) or losses (-) on SDRs and foreign exchange, as well as interest earned on assets.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [832, 276, 1486, 549], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-1 presents the assets, liabilities, and capital of the fund. The figures are in U.S. dollars or their equivalents based on current exchange rates computed according to the accrual method of accounting. The capital account represents the original capital appropriated to the fund by Congress of $2 billion, minus a subsequent transfer of $1.8 billion to pay for the initial U.S. quota subscription to the International Monetary Fund. Gains and losses are reflected in the cumulative net income (+) or loss (-) account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 556, 1490, 771], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"Table ESF-2 shows the results of operations by quarter. Figures are in U.S. dollars or their equivalents computed according to the accrual method. \\\"Profit (+) or loss (-) on foreign exchange\\\" includes realized profits or losses. \\\"Adjustment for change in valuation of SDR holdings and allocations\\\" reflects net gain or loss on revaluation of SDR holdings and allocations for the quarter.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [368, 842, 1259, 882], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"TABLE ESF-1.\\u2014Balances as of Dec. 31, 2006, and Mar. 31, 2007\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [455, 898, 1173, 922], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"[In thousands of dollars. Source: Office of the Assistant Secretary of the Treasury for Management]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 936, 1488, 1850], \"page_id\": 106}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Assets, liabilities, and capital</th><th>Dec. 31, 2006</th><th>Jan. 1, 2007, through Mar. 31, 2007</th><th>Mar. 31, 2007</th></tr><tr><td><b>Assets</b></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>U.S. dollars:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Held with Treasury:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>U.S. Government securities</td><td>15,884,168</td><td>183,129</td><td>16,067,297</td></tr><tr><td>Special drawing rights 1</td><td>8,870,087</td><td>77,440</td><td>8,947,527</td></tr><tr><td>Foreign exchange and securities:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>European euro</td><td>12,381,371</td><td>273,888</td><td>12,655,259</td></tr><tr><td>Japanese yen</td><td>7,946,438</td><td>107,236</td><td